ure Life at Accenture\n  * [Working here ][60]\n  * [Benefits ][61]\n  * [Work environment ][62]\n  * [Careers blog ][63]\n  How we hire How we hire\n  * [Using AI ][64]\n  * [Hiring journey ][65]\n  * [Pro tips ][66]\n* [Contact Us][67]\n* [Careers][68]\n* [Locations][69]\n* [\n  linkedin\n  ][70]\n* [\n  facebook\n  ][71]\n* [\n  instagram\n  ][72]\n[\nSearch\n][73]\nIndia\n\nCurrent Country: United States\n* Default (English)\n* All COUNTRIES & LANGUAGES\n* [Argentina (Spanish)][74]\n* [Australia (English)][75]\n* [Austria (German) ][76]\n* [Belgium (English)][77]\n* [Brazil (Portuguese)][78]\n* [Bulgaria (English)][79]\n* [Canada (English)][80]\n* [Canada (French) ][81]\n* [Chile (Spanish)][82]\n* [China/Hong Kong SAR (English)][83]\n* [China/Mainland (Chinese)][84]\n* [China/Mainland (English)][85]\n* [Colombia (Spanish)][86]\n* [Costa Rica (English)][87]\n* [Czech Republic (English)][88]\n* [Denmark (English)][89]\n* [Finland (English)][90]\n* [France (French)][91]\n* [Germany (German)][92]\n* [Greece (English)][93]\n* [Hungary (English)][94]\n* [India (English)][95]\n* [Indonesia (English)][96]\n* [Ireland (English)][97]\n* [Israel (English)][98]\n* [Italy (Italian)][99]\n* [Japan (Japanese)][100]\n* [Latvia (English)][101]\n* [Luxembourg (English)][102]\n* [Malaysia (English)][103]\n* [Mauritius (English)][104]\n* [Mexico (Spanish)][105]\n* [Morocco (English)][106]\n* [Netherlands (English)][107]\n* [New Zealand (English)][108]\n* [Norway (English)][109]\n* [Philippines (English)][110]\n* [Poland (English)][111]\n* [Poland (Polish)][112]\n* [Portugal (Portuguese)][113]\n* [Romania (English)][114]\n* [Saudi Arabia (English)][115]\n* [Singapore (English)][116]\n* [Slovakia (English)][117]\n* [South Africa (English)][118]\n* [Spain (Spanish)][119]\n* [Sweden (English)][120]\n* [Switzerland (English)][121]\n* [Thailand (English)][122]\n* [UAE (English)][123]\n* [United Kingdom (English)][124]\n* [USA (English)][125]\n\n# Together We Reinvented\n\nClose\nAnnouncement\nAccenture launches Accenture Edge to help mid-market companies harness AI and reinvent how they\noperate\n\nA new business from Accenture, built to help mid-market companies adopt AI and modernize their\ntechnology through pre-built solutions, specialist teams and leading ecosystem partnerships.\n\n[\nExpand\n][126]\nClose\nResearch Report\nAI agents are changing how consumers choose\n\nConsumers are open to delegating decisions to AI agents. See how this shift reshapes value, loyalty\nand what it takes for brands to stay chosen.\n\n[\nExpand\n][127]\nClose\nResearch Report\nApplied creativity—and how to lead it\n\nEvery company starts with an idea. They end when they run out of ideas. Or, more likely, can't\nexecute the ones they have.\n\n[\nExpand\n][128]\nClose\nPerspective\nPower first: The new playbook for data center development\n\nAI is pushing power demand beyond grid limits. Winning data center developers are shifting to a\npower-first strategy, securing capacity early, aligning with utilities, and designing for\nflexibility.\n\n[\nExpand\n][129]\nClose\nPerspective\nAI for commodity trading: Signals, speed and share of value\n\nAs volatility reshapes commodity markets, leading firms are leveraging AI to sharpen trading\nsignals, optimize execution, and scale a structural advantage across the value chain.\n\n[\nExpand\n][130]\nClose\nResearch Report\nReinventing for Human + AI Engineering\n\nIs your engineering function a cost center or a growth engine? Our research shows what leading\ncompanies are doing differently to compress cycle times, improve launch reliability and build\ncompounding advantage.\n\n[\nExpand\n][131]\nClose\nPerspective\nAI agents are rewriting the platform playbook\n\nWhy agentic commerce changes how consumer and advertising platforms create value\n\n[\nExpand\n][132]\nClose\nResearch Report\nRedefining Resilience: To survive new threats, leaders must address a perception gap\n\nIn today’s AI driven threat landscape, cyber resilience is a strategic mandate. See 5 actions\nleaders can align on to ensure their business keeps running when—not if—disruption happens.\n\n[\nExpand\n][133]\nCarousel slider control\n\n#### “Companies will have a greater technology landscape, but we need to completely change the\n#### narrative to inspire people to paint the future. It is human in the lead, not human in the\n#### loop.”\n\nJulie Sweet\n\n## 360° VALUE\n\n### Every day, we embrace change and create value for all our stakeholders around the world.\n\n[\nSee the report\n][134]\nplay automatic slide show\npause automatic slide show\nshow previous slide\nslideText 1 ofText / 1\nshow next slide\n\n### YMCA turns crisis into capability at scale\n\nYMCA partnered with Accenture to build a community-based model that helps refugees and displaced\npeople gain skills, find work, and rebuild their futures—moving from relief to long-term capability.\n\n[\nRead more\n][135]\n\n### How UNICEF's GenU is closing the youth skills gap\n\nThrough UNICEF’s partnership with Accenture, young people gain access to AI-powered skilling,\ndigital learning and entrepreneurship opportunities that connect them to employment and brighter\nfutures.\n\n[\nRead more\n][136]\n\n### Philipstown's wire cars go global\n\nPhilipstown’s wire car tradition is accelerating onto the global stage through immersive\nstorytelling, gaming and commerce—fueling opportunity and driving impact far beyond the track.\n\n[\nRead more\n][137]\n\n### Google Cloud reimagines lead enrichment with agentic AI\n\nThe leading hyperscaler replaced batch processing with an agentic model that delivers decision-ready\noutputs up to 30x faster—sharpening prioritization while enabling more confident sales decisions.\n\n[\nRead more\n][138]\n\n### Bristol Myers Squibb scales AI to rewire everyday work\n\nThe life sciences leader is putting people at the center of its AI ambition—rewiring work across the\nenterprise to empower employees, drive innovation and accelerate the delivery of therapies to\npatients.\n\n[\nRead more\n][139]\n\n## Global recognition and awards\n\nToggle awards card detail view\n\n### A Leader in Reinvention\n\nOur Chair and CEO, Julie Sweet, is No. 11 on Fortune’s Most Powerful People in Business. Every day,\nJulie and our people demonstrate why Accenture is our clients’ reinvention partner of choice.\n\n[\nSee related awards\n][140]\nToggle awards card detail view\n\n### A Great Place To Work®\n\nWe are very proud to have earned the No. 4 spot on the Great Place To Work® list of the World’s Best\nWorkplaces™, our highest-ever ranking on this prestigious list.\n\nThis recognition is especially meaningful because it is based on feedback from our people worldwide.\n\n[\nSee related awards\n][141]\nToggle awards card detail view\n\n### A Trusted Industry Leader\n\nAccenture is a Leader in the 2025 Gartner Magic Quadrant for Public Cloud IT Transformation\nServices.\n\nAccenture placed highest on the Ability to Execute axis in the Magic Quadrant report, which assessed\na total of 15 PCITS providers.\n\n[\nSee related awards\n][142]\nCareers\n\n### Build a career that's as exciting as the world we're shaping\n\nGrow personally and professionally in a global company that helps you unlock your full potential.\n\n[\nJoin us\n][143]\nAccenture news\nPlay\nPause\n[\n\nJuly 15, 2026\n\n### Accenture Helps European Commission’s Directorate-General for International Partnerships to\n### Scale AI Across Global Operations\n\n][144]\n[\n\nJuly 7, 2026\n\n### NATO Announces Major Contract with Accenture to Help Advance Towards a More Agile and Resilient\n### Digital Infrastructure\n\n][145]\n[\n\nJune 29, 2026\n\n### ServiceNow and Accenture Launch AI-powered Services to Accelerate the Shift from Legacy Risk\n### Platforms to Agentic AI\n\n][146]\n[\n\nJune 30, 2026\n\n### Europe Accelerates in AI Race But a Growing Divide Threatens Progress\n\n][147]\n[\n\nJune 17, 2026\n\n### Accenture to Strengthen Capabilities for Sof