 * [HIMSS 2026][206]\n* [About us][207]\n  * [Who we are][208]\n    * [Ascom Mission, Vision, Values][209]\n    * [Corporate strategy][210]\n    * [Board of Directors][211]\n    * [Executive Management][212]\n  * [Why Ascom][213]\n    * [Interoperability partners][214]\n    * [Your OEM partner][215]\n    * [Channel partners ][216]\n  * [Corporate Governance][217]\n    * [Quality certification][218]\n    * [Directives and Guidelines][219]\n    * [Product Security][220]\n  * [Sustainability][221]\n    * [UN SDGs][222]\n  * [Work at Ascom][223]\n* [Investors][224]\n  * [Investors Relations Information][225]\n  * [Business Profile][226]\n  * [Share information][227]\n  * [Major shareholders][228]\n  * [Share buyback program][229]\n  * [Shareholder FAQ][230]\n  * [Reports and presentations][231]\n  * [Annual General Meeting][232]\n  * [Financial calendar][233]\n  * [Analyst coverage][234]\n* [Contact us][235]\n\n# Bringing data to life\n\nIntegrated communication and collaboration solutions for enhanced safety and efficiency\n\n[\nHospitals and acute care\n][236][\nLong-term care\n][237][\nEnterprise\n][238]\n\n## Mobility with confidence\n\nMobility isn’t just about movement - it’s about confidence in every step\n\n[Find out more][239]\n[Nurse looking at data on myco4 phone]\n\n## We work every day to bring data to life\n\nEvery single second, Ascom systems generate 1.3 million data points. We are here to turn these into\nuseful and actionable information for people in the toughest operational environments – and assist\nthem to make the best possible decisions.\n\nWith solutions for [Clinical Surveillance][240], [Rapid response][241], [Alarm Management][242],\n[Smart Nurse call systems][243], [Mobile Devices, ][244][Staff Safety][245] and [Activity\nmonitoring][246] – we make a difference every day, helping people care for others and keeping them\nsafe.\n\n[Find out more][247]\n\n## When accuracy isn’t optional\n\n## The era of ventilator integration to the patient record\n\nSheffield Teaching Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust is one of the UK’s biggest providers of integrated\nhospital and community-based healthcare, offering a comprehensive range of local and tertiary\nservices. Within the organization, the Neonatal Intensive Care Unit (NICU) plays a critical role in\ncaring for the most vulnerable patients—newborns requiring advanced medical support due to\nprematurity, congenital conditions, or severe illness.\n\n[Read the full story][248]\n[Play] Your browser does not support HTML5 video.\n\n## Digital Transformation at Frosinone\n\nAs healthcare digitalizes, managing both clinical and personal alarms is key to ensuring safety,\nprompt responses, and high-quality care. The experience of the Frosinone Local Health Authority in\nItaly demonstrates how a structured approach can be adopted to coordinate the management of patient\nsafety events and incidents related to the protection of healthcare staff.\n\n[Read the full article ][249]\n\n## Employee protection as a competitive advantage\n\nDiscover why protecting lone workers is now essential for retention and compliance. Learn how\nreal‑time emergency response, man‑down alarms, and dedicated safety devices can strengthen your\norganization’s safety culture.\n\n[Unlock the full story][250]\n\n## Reliable communication in explosive environments\n\nCommunication in ATEX classified environments is never just about a tool. It is the first line of\ndefense that protects people, supports compliance, and keeps operations under control. Newchem, a\nleading Italian producer of active pharmaceutical ingredients, understands this reality. With the\nAscom solution, Newchem moved from broad warnings to clear alerts that support immediate action.\nFire safety systems, monitoring systems, and production equipment now connect into a single\nenvironment that routes the right information to the right people at the right time.\n\n[Read the case][251]\nLatest news\nFind the latest financial and business news\nJune 19, 2026\n[Ascom completes its Share Buyback Program][252]\nAd hoc announcement pursuant to Art. 53 LRBaar, Switzerland, June 19, 2026\nMarch 9, 2026\n[Ascom reports solid 2025 full-year results][253]\nAd hoc announcement pursuant to Art. 53 LRBaar, Switzerland, 9 March 2026\n[See all news][254]\n\n### Customer stories\n\n[\nSant Joan de Déu Barcelona, Spain\n\nA case study demonstrating the reduction of medical device alarms in the pediatric ICU of Sant Joan\nde Déu Barcelona Teaching Hospital—through Ascom’s Alarm Management & Clinical Monitoring solution.\n\nHospital\n\n][255]\n[\nHarrogate and District NHS Foundation Trust, UK\n\nA case study demonstrating how Ascom's Smart Nurse Call solution helped improve patient outcomes,\nstaff workloads and hospital costs at Harrogate and District NHS Foundation Trust.\n\nHospital\n\n][256]\n[\nWestag, Germany\n\nWorking together with the customer as a trusted, long-term partner, Ascom has helped Westag improve\nstaff communication and boost workplace and lone worker safety, while also playing a vital role in\nthe digitalization of many of their processes.\n\nIndustry\n\n][257]\n[Read all customer stories][258]\n\n## News\n\n[Ad hoc announcements][259]\n[Business News][260]\n\n## Let's talk\n\nPlease keep me informed about new publications, solutions, trends or useful information related to\nthis topic. I understand I can unsubscribe at any time.\nGet in touch\n\nBy submitting the form you give consent to store your [personal data][261].\n\n## Thank you!\n\n[NO MESSAGE]\nSubscribe to our financial newsletter\n* [Work at Ascom][262]\n* [Your OEM partner][263]\n* [Investors][264]\n* [Ascom Portal Access][265]\n[Mobile devices][266]\n* [Smartphones][267]\n* [Pagers][268]\n[Software][269]\n* [Digistat clinical software ][270]\n* [Unite communications software][271]\n* [Ofelia software][272]\n[Nurse call and monitoring systems][273]\n* [teleCARE IP for care homes][274]\n* [Telligence for hospitals][275]\nAscom Hol